# Next.js Architecture

- Stack baseline: Next.js App Router + React + TypeScript strict + Tailwind v4.
- Keep route entries in `app/**/page.tsx` and global shell in `app/layout.tsx`.
- Use route groups `(group)` only for organization, not URL changes.

## Server vs Client

- Server Components are default.
- Add `"use client"` only for hooks, browser APIs, or direct interaction logic.
- Avoid making whole pages client components unless absolutely required.
- Keep client islands focused (navigation behavior, FAQ toggles, consent dialog).

## Dynamic Routes

- For static data-driven details (`[slug]`), implement `generateStaticParams`.
- Resolve invalid params with `notFound()`.
- Prefer static rendering for marketing/content pages unless dynamic APIs are required.

## Page Composition

- Compose page sections inside `<main>`.
- Reuse `Section` wrapper for consistent spacing/container/background behavior.
- Keep section markers for readability (Hero, Benefits, FAQ, CTA).
- Place optional `Breadcrumb` near page top for subpages.

## Metadata

- Keep global metadata in root layout.
- Add route-level metadata when page intent differs significantly.
